{% doc %}
  @param {string} email - The email address
  @param {string} host - The host URL
  @param {number} [valid_for] - Token validity duration in HOURS
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  comment
    The lifetime is one hour, which is what this flow has always issued: the
    argument below was never passed on to the query, so the token lifetime came
    from the default declared in user/find.graphql instead. That default is now
    gone and the value is stated here, deliberately unchanged.

    Note the three numbers that used to disagree: this file defaulted to 5 and
    documented minutes, the graphql declared 48 hours, and what shipped was one
    hour. Pick the intended lifetime here if one hour is not it.
  endcomment
  assign valid_for = valid_for | default: 1
  function user = 'modules/user/queries/user/find', email: email, with_token: true, id: null, expires_in: valid_for

  assign object = {
    "email": email,
    "id": user.id,
    "token": user.token,
    "host": host
  }

  return object
%}
